WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.837
`- They know us in Paris.

00:00:01.837 --> 00:00:03.270
[members speaking French]

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.572
We're a band named Cortis.
Please search it up.

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:09.322
[exciting music]

00:00:13.795 --> 00:00:15.545
- [Woman] Come on in.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.166
- Hey, "Vogue" this is -

00:00:19.166 --> 00:00:20.200
- [All] Cortis.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.480
- And we're here in Paris.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.340
Two members are missing right now

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.970
and I think they will
join us like later on.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.760
- So we're gonna order
some coffee and drinks.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.720
- Yeah, we're in Paris,

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.520
so we need to drink some
cold coffee, I guess.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.601
[upbeat music]

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.171
- [Barista] Really French is an espresso.

00:00:37.171 --> 00:00:38.940
- Espresso?
- Espresso.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.620
- Showy.
[laughs]

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.598
- That's...

00:00:41.598 --> 00:00:44.610
- I've never tried it before,
but I'll get espresso.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.152
- Yeah, I'll get it.

00:00:46.152 --> 00:00:46.985
- Espresso?

00:00:46.985 --> 00:00:50.110
- Yes. And also vanilla ice cream.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.752
- [Barista] Okay.

00:00:51.752 --> 00:00:53.610
- Yeah. Thank you. Thank
you. [speaks French].

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.070
- Oh, I'm nervous.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:55.950
[laughs]

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:59.070
- After this, I definitely
need the ice cream.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:02.190
- Yeah.
- Oh, whoa.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:03.480
- It's very strong.
[laughs]

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.523
- Yeah. Very strong. Thank you.

00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:06.570
- Thank you. Thank you.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:07.860
- James loves dessert.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.710
Sometimes he doesn't like eat food.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:14.130
I don't understand that,
but that's his style so.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:15.240
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.860
- Let me try it. Oh.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:21.758
- It's melting. I prefer this way. Yeah.

00:01:21.758 --> 00:01:24.627
- Yeah, we needed something sweet. Oh.

00:01:24.627 --> 00:01:27.592
- Oh. Hey.

00:01:27.592 --> 00:01:32.159
[members greeting each other in French]

00:01:32.159 --> 00:01:34.974
- We're going to record shop in Paris.

00:01:34.974 --> 00:01:35.807
- All right.

00:01:35.807 --> 00:01:36.648
- Okay, okay.

00:01:36.648 --> 00:01:38.460
[light music]

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.470
- Paris, yeah, it has its own vibe.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:42.780
It has its own feeling to it

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:46.020
and I think it's a very inspiring city.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.000
- This is my first time in Paris

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.245
and it's the group's first time

00:01:49.245 --> 00:01:50.850
in Paris.
- Yes.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:52.380
- First time in Europe, actually.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:57.120
- The buildings, they're like beautiful.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.250
- Everything's like beautiful.
- And like on the way I saw

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:03.360
like a couple just randomly sitting

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:06.150
in front of a building and
it just looked romantic.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.019
It's just a vibe. It's true.

00:02:08.019 --> 00:02:10.680
- Everything looks like
a scene in a movie.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.360
- All right, guys, let's
go see this record store.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.193
- There it is.

00:02:14.146 --> 00:02:15.661
- Plastic Soul Records.

00:02:15.661 --> 00:02:18.330
- Oh, Plastic Soul Records.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:19.853
- Oh, they got the classics.

00:02:19.853 --> 00:02:22.380
[upbeat music]

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:25.650
- We listen to every kinds
of, every kinds of music.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:29.640
- As long as it's new to
us, it's a new experience,

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.866
we try to kind of accept it as it is.

00:02:32.866 --> 00:02:35.190
[light music]

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:37.860
- I used to listen to Debussy in Korea.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:42.860
To feel the vibe, I started
listening to Debussy again.

00:02:43.874 --> 00:02:46.890
- This is my favorite
Rolling Stones album.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:50.310
Stop playing with me.
"Exile on Main Street."

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.220
I've been listening to "Rocks Off."

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.570
This is a beautiful album.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:57.879
- I want to try these two. Ralph Sutton.

00:02:57.879 --> 00:02:59.970
Thank you so much.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:00.803
[speaks French]

00:03:00.803 --> 00:03:01.636
- "La Vie en rose."

00:03:01.636 --> 00:03:05.220
This is one of the most
famous singers in France

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.580
and it was the 1962 first print.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:13.580
- Celine Dion. CD is my
mother's spiritual mother

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:18.890
and she loves Celine Dion
and yeah, it passed on to me.

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:22.770
- So we got some good records

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:26.247
and we're moving on to the
acai shop to get some goodies.

00:03:26.247 --> 00:03:27.580
- Acai in Paris.

00:03:28.624 --> 00:03:29.541
- Let's go.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:33.339
- Paris very different from Seoul.

00:03:33.339 --> 00:03:34.530
- Yeah. I think Paris and Seoul,

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:38.490
they're both very big cities, I guess.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.911
But I think Seoul is a bit...

00:03:40.911 --> 00:03:42.110
- Bike, bikes!

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:46.710
- ...a bit more modern compared to Paris

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:49.923
and Paris is a bit more classic.

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.917
- Hello You. Hello.
- Hello me. Hello.

00:03:57.584 --> 00:03:58.607
- Have a nice day.

00:03:58.607 --> 00:03:59.760
- Have a good one.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.910
- We're popping out in
Paris with acai bowls.

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:06.570
- The reason why we are eating
acai bowls, even in Paris,

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:09.450
because acai bowl is our favorite food.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:13.560
- Paris is the city of love.
You gotta do what you love.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.960
- When we were making the second album,

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.990
we were really into acai bowl,

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:22.950
like we had it almost
like every day a week.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:25.530
- We noticed that the base gotta be good

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:28.590
to be a good acai.
- Yeah.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:29.423
- Acai bowl.

00:04:29.423 --> 00:04:31.020
- All the toppings,
they're just decorations.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.038
- They're decorations.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:32.871
- You gotta have a good base.

00:04:32.871 --> 00:04:33.810
- After we noticed that,

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.330
we started to resonate with acai bowls.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.230
It sounds weird, right?

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:41.310
But like we kind of wanted to
talk about it in our lyrics.

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:43.080
We wanna be the acai bowl,

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:46.350
the base itself, like something good.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.450
Adventurous eater is probably James

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.760
because he just puts
me onto a lot of stuff.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.680
Even this morning he was eating panini,

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.054
which I've never tried.
- Yes.

00:04:54.054 --> 00:04:58.230
- And Keonho and Seonghyeon
will be the pickiest because...

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.300
- The youngest and pickiest.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:05.190
- One French food I really want
to try, a very good Eclair.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:08.400
- For me, like before we on stage,

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:13.290
I think I... I think I take a nap a lot.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:16.278
After you take a nap, you can like feel

00:05:16.278 --> 00:05:17.160
[speaks Korean]

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:19.200
- It feels like your brain was on restart.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.430
- Yeah, restarts.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:21.900
- No matter how much you're tired,

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:24.870
I think like as soon as
you go on the stage...

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:25.890
- You're forgetting that.

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:27.870
- My mode kind of change, you know?

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:30.510
- Meeting the fans,
getting engaged with them,

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:33.153
it's just always a different experience.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.670
- Guys ready to go to the vintage store?

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:38.220
- Yeah, it's a good one. Let's go.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:39.930
- [Woman] What words do
you know in French, guys?

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:41.737
- Nothing. I only know [speaks French]

00:05:41.737 --> 00:05:43.379
[members speak French]

00:05:43.379 --> 00:05:46.546
[woman speaks French]

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:50.720
- [Woman] That means I don't speak French.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.970
[members speak French]

00:05:56.894 --> 00:05:59.394
[jazzy music]

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:03.540
- I think like almost every clothes we buy

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:05.520
is vintage, I guess.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:08.130
- When the clothes have stories to it

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:11.610
and then like certain designer
made it in certain year

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:13.290
and it becomes an archive piece.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:15.780
- That's the reason why we go
crazy about vintage clothes,

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:17.520
like the history.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:21.090
- Kurt Cobain once said this,
but it's like finding gems.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:22.530
- I feel like vintage market

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:24.870
is like just getting bigger in Korea.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:25.703
- Yes.

00:06:25.703 --> 00:06:27.420
- But like in here, Paris, it's like

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:28.992
already all over the place, so...

00:06:28.992 --> 00:06:31.742
[peaceful music]

00:06:34.634 --> 00:06:36.420
- [Saleswoman] Can you
describe James's style?

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:37.253
- James? Oh.

00:06:37.253 --> 00:06:38.130
- Rock band T-shirts.

00:06:38.965 --> 00:06:39.990
- Rock band T-shirts.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:42.930
- I think he custom make up...

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:46.170
- He crops. He crops his T-shirts.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:48.420
- Distressed.
- Yeah, he cuts everywhere.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:49.770
- Next victim.

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:52.740
- He has certain fits that he wear

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:56.011
and he got his own hairstyle going on.

00:06:56.011 --> 00:06:57.420
- Hairstyle.
[members chuckle]

00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:59.563
- Yeah, hairstyle is part
of fashion so like...

00:06:59.563 --> 00:07:01.470
- I think I can copy it.

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:02.640
- Very edged.

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:04.683
- He always got the edgy hairline.

00:07:04.683 --> 00:07:06.720
- I think he, he got this edgy.

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:09.630
- Yeah, he always got
like one part dangling.

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:11.820
Kind of pisses me off, but...
- Why?

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:13.020
- I don't know.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:17.310
He always be just narrowing
that thing down, bro.

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:18.294
- I respect you.

00:07:18.294 --> 00:07:20.096
That's your style. That's your style.

00:07:20.096 --> 00:07:21.120
- I mess with you.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.620
[light music]

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.460
- What piece would you choose, bro?

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.400
- Something like this.
[members laugh]

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:30.233
- Awesome.

00:07:30.233 --> 00:07:32.490
- Yeah. Wanna wear it?
- Flamboyant. Balenciaga.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:35.520
- Fab, fabulous.
- Orange one-piece.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:38.820
- Actually, one-pieces
kind of look really comfy.

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:40.320
- It's gonna look great on you.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:41.880
- Am I putting this on?
[members laugh]

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:45.760
- Okay. Next piece. Me?

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:46.923
Me for him.

00:07:47.957 --> 00:07:49.500
- [Saleswoman] You look great.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.669
- Why, why are you so worried?

00:07:51.669 --> 00:07:52.680
- I'm nervous. I'm nervous.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:54.803
- I'm not doing you like Juhoon did to me.

00:07:54.803 --> 00:07:55.776
- Okay. Okay.

00:07:55.776 --> 00:07:56.971
- Here you go.

00:07:56.971 --> 00:07:57.804
[laughs]

00:07:57.804 --> 00:07:58.637
- It's a swimsuit. Okay, cool.

00:07:58.637 --> 00:07:59.470
- Swimsuit.

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:00.303
- So you swim.

00:08:00.303 --> 00:08:01.333
- [All] Oh!

00:08:01.333 --> 00:08:02.592
- I got you right there.

00:08:02.592 --> 00:08:03.882
- Oh yes.

00:08:03.882 --> 00:08:05.833
- You got a swimsuit. Gucci swimsuit.

00:08:05.833 --> 00:08:06.666
- A swimmer.

00:08:06.666 --> 00:08:08.283
- Yo, I got him so right.

00:08:11.083 --> 00:08:11.916
- All right.

00:08:11.916 --> 00:08:13.909
- All right, I think it's
time to hop on a cruise.

00:08:13.909 --> 00:08:16.158
- Cruise.
- All right.

00:08:16.158 --> 00:08:18.658
[light music]

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:21.543
- Gotta take them pics for the fans.

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:25.236
We in Paris!

00:08:25.236 --> 00:08:27.736
[light music]

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:30.350
Feeling the air of Paris

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:32.910
is just the best part
of the trip, I guess.

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:35.280
- I'm looking forward to see

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:39.150
how much we're gonna take
inspiration and ideas

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:42.869
from like this trip here
and put it in our art.

00:08:42.869 --> 00:08:45.369
[light music]

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:49.771
- They know us?
- Hello. Hi.

00:08:49.771 --> 00:08:51.120
[members speak French]

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.446
- Yeah, they're saying Cortis.

00:08:52.446 --> 00:08:53.653
[speaks French]

00:08:53.653 --> 00:08:55.755
- Oh my God.
- Hey.

00:08:55.755 --> 00:08:56.832
[speaks French]

00:08:56.832 --> 00:08:58.121
- Yah, Cortis.

00:08:58.121 --> 00:08:58.954
- Hey!

00:09:03.456 --> 00:09:05.010
- I don't know. I don't
have any word of advice.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:08.139
I don't want to say the
cliche be yourself thing.

00:09:08.139 --> 00:09:09.990
It helps, but...

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:13.440
- I think you gotta find it yourself.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:17.451
Advice doesn't work if you can't feel it.

00:09:17.451 --> 00:09:18.990
- Exactly, right.

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:23.550
- In our generations, we kind
of lose track of dreaming

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:26.220
and just like sometimes
you think it's corny.

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:28.620
Sometimes you think it's just too cheesy,

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:30.443
but I think you really should.

00:09:30.443 --> 00:09:33.931
You just should. You got to
live by something, you know?

00:09:33.931 --> 00:09:36.431
[light music]

00:09:42.367 --> 00:09:45.158
- [All] Bye, Vogue.
[group shouts in French]

00:09:45.158 --> 00:09:46.325
- Yay!
- Yeah.

00:09:48.465 --> 00:09:50.470
[group claps]

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:52.970
[light music]

